A(f"1. **Front-view jaw line.** After r2 the visible jaw line (strongest light->dark step per column, lip-avoiding search window) is within {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l']['jaw_line_z_err_vs_plate_mean_mm']:.1f} mm of the plate's on average over |x| <= 60 mm (max {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l']['jaw_line_z_err_vs_plate_max_mm']:.1f} mm; the first Micro1l install had {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l_r1']['jaw_line_z_err_vs_plate_mean_mm']:.1f} / {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l_r1']['jaw_line_z_err_vs_plate_max_mm']:.1f} mm: its chin edge sat 5-8 mm above the plate's, which is the 'chin separated from the jawline' look), and its contrast matches the plate's mean ({fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l']['edge_contrast_mean_lum']:.0f} vs {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l']['plate_edge_contrast_mean_lum']:.0f} luminance units). The remaining difference is at |x| 30-40 where our edge is still 2-4 mm above the plate's stubble-pigment edge (we keep the crest on the jaw, not on the neck).")
A(f"2. **Shading tilt.** Part of the edge definition is lighting-only (custom-normal tilt <= {sb['max_extra_tilt_deg']:.1f} deg on {sb['verts_gt_1deg']} vertices, FBX normals = Import so Unity shows it; a re-normalising importer setting would remove it). Geometric crest <= {jc['max_geometric_crest_mm']:.2f} mm.")
A(f"3. **Plates disagree** at the chin by 3-4 mm (front plate: lower, U-shaped; both 3/4 plates: smaller / higher chin). 3/4 jaw + cheek edges within 3 mm: {q3['within_3mm']['start']} (start) -> {q3['within_3mm']['now']} of {q3['within_3mm']['of']}; jaw-bottom rows 566-578 mean |error| {q3['jaw_bottom_rows_566_578_mean_abs_mm']['start']:.2f} -> {q3['jaw_bottom_rows_566_578_mean_abs_mm']['now']:.2f} mm. The r2 chin crest costs the 3/4 chin-bottom contour ~0.25 mm versus the first install's 2.19 mm; front half-width and profile outlines are unchanged or better.")
A("4. **Face_M changed (disclosed):** only the lip + mouth-seam paint strips (re-laid twice: first install, r2); the lips request makes it necessary because the strips must follow the lip surface and the traced plate curves. Unity colours in `HeroBaseMaleFormProof.cs` `FaceSlots`: `Lip` (.76,.52,.43)/.42 -> (.94,.64,.48)/.30, `LipUp` (.60,.38,.31) -> (.757,.493,.333)/.30, `Seam` (.30,.15,.11)/.30 -> (.42,.18,.10)/.28 (rollback copies in `baseline/`). The lip colours are tuned for the default Tan skin (the face paint is not recoloured by the other skin tones - existing limitation).")
A("5. **Not touched (known residuals, not in this brief):** the dark nasolabial line beside one nose wing, expression / smile, ears, eyes, brows, nape / pelvis, neck cage band z 1.40-1.44, the plate's mouth-corner shading. Stubble stays a preview until the skin has UVs / a vertex-colour path.")
A("6. The eye-gate lines are my reading of the proof sheets; the numbers above are supporting measurements, not the gate.")
